\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=10D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-(5{\\pi }^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +10\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )-(-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+10(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =(5{\\pi }^{2}+7-10)-(-7+10) \\\\  & =5{\\pi }^{2}-3-3 \\\\  & =5{\\pi }^{2}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534510 true] [17592186292570 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292571 13194139534510 true] [17592186292570 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534510 true] [17592186292570 1041 "field-1" 13194139534510 true] [17592186292570 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292571 13194139534510 true] [17592186292570 1110 #uuid "a7f9b512-3f1c-52c7-9180-a7cc97446cd3" 13194139534510 true] [17592186292571 1034 "5\\pi^2-6" 13194139534510 true] [17592186292571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534510 true] [17592186292571 1111 #uuid "670ed3ae-5